# FA3 Hopper Decode / Tiny-M Investigation Report

Reference root: `/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/`

**Bottom line:** FA3 has **no separate decode/GEMV kernel**. Decode is the same warp-specialized WGMMA mainloop, with three compile-time/runtime mechanisms for tiny M: (1) **`use_one_mma_wg` → kBlockM=64 + 1 consumer WG**, (2) **Pack-GQA** to pack `seqlen_q × qhead_per_khead` into M, and (3) **split-KV** to multiply work along N and fill SMs. FA3 **accepts partial tile utilization** (padding rows still run WGMMA but skip gmem stores). Your reimpl’s 1-WG m64 with ~rep/64 real rows matches FA3’s BF16 hdim128 decode path; the bigger gap is likely **missing split-KV occupancy** and **persistent varlen scheduling**, not a missing GEMV kernel.

---

## 1. Tile Sizing for Decode

### No `seqlen_q` in the tile table — gated by `use_one_mma_wg`

`tile_size_fwd_sm90` takes **head dim + flags**, not `seqlen_q`. The decode switch is the boolean `use_one_mma_wg`, computed at runtime:

```10:14:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/heuristics.h
inline bool use_one_mma_wg(Flash_fwd_params const& params) {
    // assume pack_gqa for seqlen calculation
    return params.arch >= 90 && (params.d == 128 || params.d == 64) && !params.is_local && 
        params.seqlen_q * (params.h / params.h_k) <= 64;
};
```

**Interpretation:** “packed query length” = `seqlen_q × GQA_ratio`. When that ≤ 64 and hdim ∈ {64,128}, FA3 instantiates the **single-consumer-WG tile variant**.

Launch template wires this into a separate compiled kernel via `BOOL_SWITCH(use_one_mma_wg(...))`:

```217:221:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_launch_template.h
                BOOL_SWITCH(use_one_mma_wg(params), Use_one_mma_wg_, [&] {
                    // Avoid over compiliation by making sure this only get set if it is actually used, i.e. we currently only support one mma wg for 64/128 head dim and hopper
                    static constexpr bool Use_one_mma_wg = Use_one_mma_wg_ && Arch >= 90 && (kHeadDim == 128 || kHeadDim == 64) && (kHeadDimV == kHeadDim) && !Is_local;
                    // Only needed here to decide if we can use cluster
                    static constexpr int kBlockM = Arch >= 90 ? std::get<0>(tile_size_fwd_sm90(kHeadDim, kHeadDimV, Is_causal, Is_local, sizeof(T) /*element_size*/, V_colmajor, PagedKVNonTMA, Has_softcap, Use_one_mma_wg)) : 128;
```

### Full `tile_size_fwd_sm90` table (returns `{kBlockM, kBlockN, MmaPV_is_RS, IntraWGOverlap}`)

```10:93:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_size.h
constexpr std::tuple<int, int, bool, bool> tile_size_fwd_sm90(
        int headdim, int headdim_v, bool is_causal, bool is_local, int element_size=2,
        bool v_colmajor=false, bool paged_kv_non_TMA=false, bool softcap=false, bool use_one_mma_wg=false) {
    if (element_size == 2) {
        if (headdim <= 64) {
            // ...
            if (headdim_v == 512) {
                return {64, 64, false, false};
            } else if (headdim_v == 256) {
                return {128, 96, true, false};
            } else {
                if (use_one_mma_wg) {
                    return {64, 192, true, true};
                } else {
                    return {192, is_causal ? 128 : is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 160 : 192, is_causal || is_local, !is_local};
                }
            }
        } else if (headdim <= 96) {
            return {192, is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 144, false, true};
        } else if (headdim <= 128) {
            if (use_one_mma_wg) {
                return {64, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 176, true, true};
            } else {
                return {128, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 160, true, true};
            }
        } else if (headdim <= 192) {
            return {128, paged_kv_non_TMA || is_local ? 96 : (headdim_v <= 128 ? 128 : 96), true, true};
        } else {
            return {128, is_local ? 64 : 80, true, true};
        }
    } else {
        // FP8 path
        if (use_one_mma_wg) {
            // Decode tiles — independent of two-level accumulation setting
            if (headdim <= 96) {
                return {64, 128, true, true};
            } else {
                return {64, 96, true, true};
            }
        } else {
            // Prefill tiles ...
        }
    }
}
```

### Decode-specific tile choices (hdim128 BF16/FP16, typical vLLM decode)

| Condition | kBlockM | kBlockN (causal, dense KV) | MmaPV_is_RS | IntraWGOverlap | Consumer WGs |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `use_one_mma_wg=true` (packed M ≤ 64) | **64** | 128 | true | true | **1** |
| `use_one_mma_wg=false` (packed M > 64) | **128** | 128 | true | true | **2** |

**Examples:**
- `seqlen_q=1`, GQA=8 → packed M=8 → `use_one_mma_wg=true` → **kBlockM=64**
- `seqlen_q=4`, GQA=8 → packed M=32 → still **kBlockM=64**
- `seqlen_q=4`, GQA=32 → packed M=128 → **kBlockM=128**, 2 consumer WGs

### kBlockM never below 64 on SM90 (except LargeHeadDimV constraint)

- Minimum kBlockM in the table is **64**. No kBlockM=16/32 decode path on Hopper forward.
- FP8 explicitly labels the `use_one_mma_wg` branch **"Decode tiles"** (lines 55–61).
- **kStages = 2** hardcoded for SM90 (`flash_fwd_launch_template.h:48`); not in the tile tuple.
- **Num consumer warpgroups** derived from kBlockM, not a separate parameter:

```92:128:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    using AtomLayoutQK = Layout<Shape<Int<kBlockM / 64>, _1, _1>>;
    // ...
    static constexpr int NumMmaThreads = size(TiledMmaPV{});
    // ...
    static constexpr int NumMmaWarpGroups = NumMmaThreads / cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup;
    static_assert(NumMmaWarpGroups == 1 || NumMmaWarpGroups == 2 || NumMmaWarpGroups == 3);
```

kBlockM=64 → `AtomLayout = Shape<1,_1,_1>` → **1 consumer WG**. kBlockM=128 → **2 consumer WGs**.

